            <ArticleTitle>Facial pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>244-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Facial pain is a common symptom that may be a feature of a primary headache disorder or a secondary feature of organic disease. A thorough clinical history and physical examination may reveal the characteristic clinical features and assist in diagnosis. However, in some cases, the etiology may remain indeterminate.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
